      "title": "Nuclear modification factor in Pb-Pb in centrality bins",
      "uuid": "cd71c490-bea6-47e9-8647-b794b10cf0d0"
    }
  ],
  "data_abstract": "Measurement of W-boson production at forward rapidity in p-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} =$ 8.16 TeV and Pb-Pb collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} =$ 5.02 TeV. The measurement is done in the muon decay channel.\n\nThe fiducial region is defined by\n- $\\eta$ (pseudorapidity) of muons in $-4.0 < \\eta < -2.5$ in the laboratory frame and ALICE reference system\n- $p_{\\rm T}$ (transverse momentum) of muons larger than 10 GeV/$c$\n\nFor Pb-Pb collisions the laboratory frame and cms frame coincide. For p-Pb collisions the nucleon-nucleon cms is boosted with respect to the laboratory frame by $\\Delta y_{cms} = \\pm 0.465$ \n",
